    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d240">

                <pb facs="0328" n="208" xml:id="pg208"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">816.01/35: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Beaulac</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-12-24T10:00:00-05:45">December 24, 1931—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 1:05 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>223. Department’s 217, December 20, 1 p.m.<anchor n="34" xml:id="d240-f1"/>. The
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs has just informed me that the Government of
                    Nicaragua has decided not to recognize the present <hi rendition="#italic">de
                        facto</hi> regime in Salvador, in accordance with the clear terms of the
                    Central American treaties of 1923. Repeated to San Salvador.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Beaulac</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
